# MTLK-HERMES-EXEC US-004 — TEST-ONLY NEGATIVE fixture: image WITHOUT hermes.
#
# A synthetic image that genuinely cannot supply a `hermes` guest executable
# anywhere on the runner's composed PATH. It derives from the small upstream
# node:22-bookworm-slim runtime (the SAME node runtime the synthetic-pi fixture
# uses) so the negative imports cheaply and the multi-GB bedlam-based POSITIVE
# fixture (Dockerfile.synthetic-hermes) remains the only heavy derived image.
#
# It is deliberately NOT derived from the bedlam positive: a matchlock import of
# a bedlam-rooted image squashes a fresh ~4.8GB rootfs blob per image, which
# does not fit this host's disk budget for two extra negatives. The POSITIVE
# fixture still satisfies the "based on igorhvr/bedlam-ubuntu" requirement and
# the image-provided fake hermes lives IN the positive image only.
#
# igorhvr/bedlam-ubuntu and the real user harness are never overwritten/
# retagged/mutated; this is a NEW derived image used ONLY by the synthetic
# gate's missing-harness negative. It contains NO provider credentials and
# performs NO model calls.

FROM node:22-bookworm-slim

LABEL org.tamandua.synthetic-hermes="TEST-ONLY-missing-harness"

# node:22-bookworm-slim ships node >= 22, /bin/sh and coreutils (the guest
# bridge/runtime the packed helper pack needs). There is intentionally NO
# hermes executable here.

WORKDIR /root
CMD ["/bin/bash"]
